{"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","subject_key":"ap-calculus-ab","topic_code":"1.9","key":"A","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"A","ambiguous":false,"work":"From the table, as x approaches 1 from the left, g(x) approaches 5 (4.8, 4.98, 4.998). From the right, g(x) also approaches 5 (5.002, 5.02, 5.2). Therefore lim(x→1) g(x) = 5. Since g(1) = 2, the function has a removable discontinuity: an open circle at (1,5) and a filled point at (1,2)."},"usage":{"inputTokens":484,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":484,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":437,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":130,"reasoningTokens":307},"totalTokens":921,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":484,"completion_tokens":437,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":484,"total_tokens":921,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":307}},"reasoningTokens":307,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4154},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":["Correct choice is noticeably longer than the distractors."]},"usage":{"inputTokens":20846,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":8686,"cacheReadTokens":12160},"outputTokens":3360,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":133,"reasoningTokens":3227},"totalTokens":24206,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":20846,"completion_tokens":3360,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":12160,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":8686,"total_tokens":24206,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":12160},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3227}},"reasoningTokens":3227,"cachedInputTokens":12160},"ms":27957},"at":"2026-10-07T00:33:49.621Z"}
{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-calculus-ab","topic_code":"1.12","key":"C","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"C","ambiguous":false,"work":"To be continuous on the closed interval [-1, 3], the function must be defined and continuous at every point in this interval.\n- A: f(x) has discontinuities where x^2 - 4 = 0, which gives x = 2 and x = -2. The point x = 2 lies in [-1, 3], so it is not continuous on the interval.\n- B: f(x) = sqrt(x) is not defined for negative numbers, so it is undefined on [-1, 0).\n- C: f(x) has discontinuities where x^2 - 2x - 8 = (x - 4)(x + 2) = 0, which occurs at x = -2 and x = 4. Neither of these values lies in [-1, 3]. Since rational functions are continuous everywhere their denominator is nonzero, f is continuous on all of [-1, 3].\n- D: The piecewise function has a discontinuity at x = 1 because the left-hand limit is 1^2 = 1, while f(1) = 2(1) = 2."},"usage":{"inputTokens":302,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":302,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":636,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":270,"reasoningTokens":366},"totalTokens":938,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":366,"promptTokenCount":302,"candidatesTokenCount":270,"totalTokenCount":938,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":302}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":270}]},"reasoningTokens":366,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":6555},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":["Distractor rationales use a consistent pedagogical template ('Tempting because... Fix:...')."]},"usage":{"inputTokens":21835,"inputTokenDetails