{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-calculus-ab","topic_code":"1.14","key":"B","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"B","ambiguous":false,"work":"To determine the behavior of f(x) = 2x/(x - 3) near x = 3, analyze the one-sided limits: as x approaches 3 from the left (x < 3), the numerator approaches 6 (positive) while the denominator approaches 0 through negative values, giving lim(x→3⁻) f(x) = -∞. As x approaches 3 from the right (x > 3), the numerator approaches 6 and the denominator approaches 0 through positive values, giving lim(x→3⁺) f(x) = ∞. Since the values grow without bound, x = 3 is a vertical asymptote."},"usage":{"inputTokens":351,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":351,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":556,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":153,"reasoningTokens":403},"totalTokens":907,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":403,"promptTokenCount":351,"candidatesTokenCount":153,"totalTokenCount":907,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":351}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":153}]},"reasoningTokens":403,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5011},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":21912,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":21912,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":588,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":214,"reasoningTokens":374},"totalTokens":22500,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":374,"promptTokenCount":21912,"candidatesTokenCount":214,"totalTokenCount":22500,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":21912}],"candidatesTokensDetails"